{"id":"086b1b3d5b60a929","group":"17","path":"17/17-df-prime-model.md","title":"Prime Models and Models Prime over Parameters","display":"df-prime-model — Prime Models and Models Prime over Parameters","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-df-prime-model","aliases":["17-df-prime-model"],"display":"df-prime-model — Prime Models and Models Prime over Parameters","depends_on":["[[17-df-model]]","[[17-df-elementary-embedding]]","[[17-df-type]]","[[17-df-tuple-satisfaction]]"],"source_section":"2.3","source_result":"Prime-model definition preceding Theorem 2.3.4","source_pages_print":[99],"source_pages_djvu":[115],"source_verification":"prime-model clause compared in supplied OCR; PrimeOver is a separately checked local parameter-relative extension","label_origin":"local-catalog"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-df-prime-model"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-df-prime-model</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-prime-model — Prime Models and Models Prime over Parameters"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"16340c2187670288\" href=\"?note=16340c2187670288\" title=\"17-df-elementary-embedding\">17-df-elementary-embedding</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"07adad8c036296f7\" href=\"?note=07adad8c036296f7\" title=\"17-df-type\">17-df-type</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4ec60741c4296112\" href=\"?note=4ec60741c4296112\" title=\"17-df-tuple-satisfaction\">17-df-tuple-satisfaction</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_section","html":"2.3"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Prime-model definition preceding Theorem 2.3.4"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>99</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>115</span></div>"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"prime-model clause compared in supplied OCR; PrimeOver is a separately checked local parameter-relative extension"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span> is an <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-theory; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)\">\\(\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"16340c2187670288\" href=\"?note=16340c2187670288\" title=\"17-df-elementary-embedding\">17-df-elementary-embedding</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\">\\(\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\)</span> is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"07adad8c036296f7\" href=\"?note=07adad8c036296f7\" title=\"17-df-type\">17-df-type</a>, and tuple satisfaction is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"4ec60741c4296112\" href=\"?note=4ec60741c4296112\" title=\"17-df-tuple-satisfaction\">17-df-tuple-satisfaction</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M\">\\(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M\\)</span> are <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-structures and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> is a candidate parameter set. <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ParameterAgreement}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{ParameterAgreement}_L\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PrimeOver}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{PrimeOver}_L\\)</span> are defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{ParameterAgreement}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M,A)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;A\\subseteq|\\mathfrak P|\\cap|\\mathfrak M|\n\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\;\\forall\\bar a\\in A^n\\\\\n&amp;\\bigl(\\mathfrak P\\models\\varphi[\\bar a]\\leftrightarrow\\mathfrak M\\models\\varphi[\\bar a]\\bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L(\\mathfrak P,T)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\mathfrak P\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\n\\land\\forall\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)\\ne\\varnothing,\\\\\n\\operatorname{PrimeOver}_L(\\mathfrak P,T,A)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\mathfrak P\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\land A\\subseteq|\\mathfrak P|\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ParameterAgreement}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M,A)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{20mm}\\to\\exists f\\in\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)\\;\n\\forall a\\in A\\;(f(a)=a)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{ParameterAgreement}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M,A)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;A\\subseteq|\\mathfrak P|\\cap|\\mathfrak M|\n\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\;\\forall\\bar a\\in A^n\\\\\n&amp;\\bigl(\\mathfrak P\\models\\varphi[\\bar a]\\leftrightarrow\\mathfrak M\\models\\varphi[\\bar a]\\bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L(\\mathfrak P,T)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\mathfrak P\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\n\\land\\forall\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)\\ne\\varnothing,\\\\\n\\operatorname{PrimeOver}_L(\\mathfrak P,T,A)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\mathfrak P\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\land A\\subseteq|\\mathfrak P|\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ParameterAgreement}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M,A)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{20mm}\\to\\exists f\\in\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)\\;\n\\forall a\\in A\\;(f(a)=a)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>The parameter-free prime-model definition occurs in §2.3, printed p. 99, DjVu page 115. The parameter-relative clause is a local extension: comparison models must give every finite parameter tuple the same complete type. Equivalently, their expansions naming <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> have the same theory; carrier overlap alone does not ensure this.</p>\n<p>For example, let <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> be the complete theory of a two-element structure with one constant <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c\">\\(c\\)</span>. Take two structures on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{a,b\\}\">\\(\\{a,b\\}\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c^{\\mathfrak P}=a\">\\(c^{\\mathfrak P}=a\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c^{\\mathfrak M}=b\">\\(c^{\\mathfrak M}=b\\)</span>. The finite model <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak P\">\\(\\mathfrak P\\)</span> is prime over the parameter <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\">\\(a\\)</span> with its actual type <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x=c\">\\(x=c\\)</span>. Yet no elementary embedding from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak P\">\\(\\mathfrak P\\)</span> to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak M\">\\(\\mathfrak M\\)</span> fixes <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\">\\(a\\)</span>. The parameter-agreement condition excludes this incompatible comparison model. Under agreement, primeness is exactly primeness of the expansion naming <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span>, with embeddings required to preserve those constants.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-model","status":"resolved","id":"53255a372e5c1ee8","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-model]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-embedding","status":"resolved","id":"16340c2187670288","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-elementary-embedding]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-type","status":"resolved","id":"07adad8c036296f7","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-type]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-tuple-satisfaction","status":"resolved","id":"4ec60741c4296112","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-tuple-satisfaction]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-model","status":"resolved","id":"53255a372e5c1ee8","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L$ is an $L$-theory; $\\operatorname{Mod}(T)$ is from [[17-df-model]].","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-embedding","status":"resolved","id":"16340c2187670288","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)$ is from [[17-df-elementary-embedding]].","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-type","status":"resolved","id":"07adad8c036296f7","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}$ is from [[17-df-type]], and tuple satisfaction is from [[17-df-tuple-satisfaction]].","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-tuple-satisfaction","status":"resolved","id":"4ec60741c4296112","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}$ is from [[17-df-type]], and tuple satisfaction is from [[17-df-tuple-satisfaction]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ParameterAgreement}_L","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{PrimeOver}_L","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{ParameterAgreement}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M,A)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&A\\subseteq|\\mathfrak P|\\cap|\\mathfrak M|\n\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\;\\forall\\bar a\\in A^n\\\\\n&\\bigl(\\mathfrak P\\models\\varphi[\\bar a]\\leftrightarrow\\mathfrak M\\models\\varphi[\\bar a]\\bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L(\\mathfrak P,T)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\\mathfrak P\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\n\\land\\forall\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)\\ne\\varnothing,\\\\\n\\operatorname{PrimeOver}_L(\\mathfrak P,T,A)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\\mathfrak P\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\land A\\subseteq|\\mathfrak P|\\\\\n&\\land\\forall\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ParameterAgreement}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M,A)\\\\\n&\\hspace{20mm}\\to\\exists f\\in\\operatorname{ElemEmb}_L(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak M)\\;\n\\forall a\\in A\\;(f(a)=a)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"c","display":false},{"tex":"\\{a,b\\}","display":false},{"tex":"c^{\\mathfrak P}=a","display":false},{"tex":"c^{\\mathfrak M}=b","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathfrak P","display":false},{"tex":"a","display":false},{"tex":"x=c","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathfrak P","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathfrak M","display":false},{"tex":"a","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false}],"bytes":3065,"backlinks":[{"id":"e501f306697361a1","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L$ (prime-model predicate, see [[17-df-prime-model]])"},{"id":"6ca15fee71357037","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L$ (prime-model predicate, see [[17-df-prime-model]])"},{"id":"6738c8e9f2e3c32e","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L$ (prime-model predicate, see [[17-df-prime-model]])"},{"id":"b71a35c07e472b22","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{PrimeOver}_L$ (prime-over-parameters predicate, see [[17-df-prime-model]])"},{"id":"13c73c6f79ee78a7","anchor":"ref-48","locations":["正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"[[17-df-prime-model]]"},{"id":"2c98c9e634ff4b44","anchor":"ref-94","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[17-df-abstract-logic]]\n[[17-df-abstract-logic-compactness]]\n[[17-df-abstract-logic-lowenheim-skolem]]\n[[17-df-aleph-one-categoricity]]\n[[17-df-aleph-zero-categoricity]]\n[[17-df-algebraic-closure]]\n[[17-df-assignment]]\n[[17-df-assignment-predicate]]\n[[17-df-atomic-formula]]\n[[17-df-atomic-model]]\n[[17-df-atomic-model-notation]]\n[[17-df-bool-